     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi!<div><br></div><div>Is it possible to write let&#39;s say the ui.R, and I have some inputs, and some outputs, and writing them into separate files? So something like this:<br></div><div><br></div><div><pre style=\"padding:8.5px;font-family:&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Droid Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:12.025px;color:rgb(51,51,51);border-top-left-radius:4px;border-top-right-radius:4px;border-bottom-right-radius:4px;border-bottom-left-radius:4px;margin-bottom:9px;line-height:18px;word-break:break-all;word-wrap:break-word;white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:rgb(245,245,245);border:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.14902)\"><code style=\"font-family:&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Droid Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,Consolas,Monaco,monospace;color:inherit;border-top-left-radius:3px;border-top-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-left-radius:3px;background-color:transparent\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">selectInput</span><span><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">(</span></span><span><span style=\"color:rgb(3,106,7)\">&quot;dataset&quot;</span></span><span>,</span> <span><span style=\"color:rgb(3,106,7)\">&quot;Choose a dataset:&quot;</span></span><span>,</span> \r\n                <span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">choices</span> <span><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">=</span></span> <span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">c</span><span><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">(</span></span><span><span style=\"color:rgb(3,106,7)\">&quot;rock&quot;</span></span><span>,</span> <span><span style=\"color:rgb(3,106,7)\">&quot;pressure&quot;</span></span><span>,</span> <span><span style=\"color:rgb(3,106,7)\">&quot;cars&quot;</span></span><span><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">)</span><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">)</span>,</span>\r\n\r\n    <span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">numericInput</span><span><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">(</span></span><span><span style=\"color:rgb(3,106,7)\">&quot;obs&quot;</span></span><span>,</span> <span><span style=\"color:rgb(3,106,7)\">&quot;Number of observations to view:&quot;</span></span><span>,</span> <span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,205)\">10</span></span><span><span style=\"color:rgb(104,118,135)\">)</span></span></code></pre></div><div>and the selectInput would be in the ui.R, and the numericInput would be in a separate file, extender.R. I have a few Shiny application, and they have many inputs in common, and it would be nice, to just paste these common things (the first and last &quot;few&quot; lines)from a separate .R file.</div><div><br></div><div>So is it possible to just extend these files? Or any workaround?</div><div><br></div><div>Thanks in advance,</div><div>Dénes</div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
